w: 1.~God reign- eth, let the earth be glad, and isles re- joice each one.
w: 2.~Fire goes be- fore him, and his foes it burns up round a- bout:
w: 3.~Hills at the pre- sence of the Lord, like wax, did melt a- way;
w: 4.~The heav’ns de- clare his right- eous- ness, all men his glo- ry see.
w: 5.~Who do of i- dols boast them- selves, let shame up- on them fall:
w: 6.~Zi- on did hear, and joy- ful was, glad Ju- dah’s daugh- ters were;
w: 7.~For thou, O Lord, art high a- bove all things on earth that are;
w: 8.~Hate ill, all ye that love the Lord: his saints’ souls kee- peth he;
w: 9.~Fo- r all those that be right- eous sown is a joy- ful light,
w: 10.~Ye right- eous, in the Lord re- joice; ex- press your thank- ful- ness,
