w: Dark clouds him com- pass; and in right with judg- ment dwells his throne.
w: His ligh- tnings ligh- ten did the world; earth saw, and shook through- out.
w: Ev’n at the pre- sence of the Lord of all the earth, I say.
w: All who serve gra- ven i- ma- ges, con- found- ed let them be.
w: Ye that are call- èd gods, see that ye do him wor- ship all.
w: They much re- joiced, O Lord, be- cause thy judg- ments did ap- pear.
w: A- bove all o- ther gods thou art ex- alt- ed ver- y far.
w: And from the hands of wi- cked men he sets them safe and free.
w: And glad- ness sown is for all those that are in heart u- pright.
w: When ye in- to your me- mo- ry do call his ho- li- ness.
